Core Creative: Use a top-tier life-and-death crisis atmosphere to package an extremely ordinary cooking scene. Utilize extreme lighting changes, costume mismatches, and actor facial expressions to create a hilarious ''insane'' contrast.

Duration: 15 seconds
Scene: From an extremely oppressive, dimly blue-lit abandoned warehouse, it instantly transforms into a sunny, overly warm family kitchen.

Storyboard
00:00-00:05 Shot 1: Life-and-Death Countdown and Extreme High Pressure
Camera: Extreme macro close-ups and facial close-ups alternating, violent handheld shaking, cold cyan-blue tone.
Visual: A digital timer is frantically counting down: 00:04, 00:03. Large beads of sweat roll down a man''s forehead. He is wearing extremely heavy, professional green bomb disposal gear and a tactical helmet, his hands trembling as he holds a huge pair of pliers, staring intensely at the intertwined red and blue wires. The atmosphere is extremely oppressive, with only heavy breathing and a loud heartbeat in the background.

00:05-00:10 Shot 2: Desperate Cut and Suffocating Pause
Camera: POV shot followed by a medium low-angle shot, extremely tense slow motion.
Action: A female assistant next to him, also in full bomb disposal gear, closes her eyes in despair, shaking her head and screaming heart-wrenchingly. The man lets out a heroic roar, closes his eyes with a look of ready-to-die resolve, and the pliers squeeze hard, cutting the red wire. The timer hits 00:00 with an extremely sharp, loud ''Beep—''. The image freezes at the moment before the explosion.

00:10-00:15 Shot 3: Silly Twist and Food Carnival
Camera: An abrupt Smash Cut to a level wide shot, with lighting instantly changing to extremely bright and warm orange-yellow Japanese drama kitchen light.
Visual: There was no bomb at all. The glowing object with the countdown turns out to be an extremely advanced smart rice cooker. As the ''beep'' ends, the rice cooker lid clicks open, gushing with thick, enticing steam. The male and female leads, who were just ready to die, are still wearing the extremely mismatched heavy bomb disposal gear, but their expressions have instantly turned into ecstatic foodies. The man flips open his helmet visor and gives a thumb up to the camera, revealing a wildly exaggerated and greasy Thai-style eight-tooth smile. The female lead suddenly has a bowl and chopsticks in her hand, staring at the rice cooker and swallowing. Colorful Thai promotional text and funny sound effects pop up crudely around the screen.','missing',3,'A tense bomb-disposal standoff builds to a screaming climax, then reveals it was never a bomb at all — just a smart rice cooker finishing its cycle, and the panicked pair turn instantly into delighted, hungry foodies.','keep','pass','direct','high','meme-comedy','photoreal','extreme macro close-ups and facial close-ups, violent handheld shaking','mixed','mixed','none',0.93,'Grounded real-world comedic bait-and-switch ad for a rice cooker; food/appliance is the payoff; honest absurd comedy genre passes authenticity.',false) on conflict (clip_id) do update set video_id=excluded.video_id, title=excluded.title, generator=excluded.generator, runtime_s=excluded.runtime_s, aspect_ratio=excluded.aspect_ratio, source_url=excluded.source_url, verbatim_prompt=excluded.verbatim_prompt, asset_status=excluded.asset_status, shot_count=excluded.shot_count, summary=excluded.summary, verdict=excluded.verdict, step1_grounded_brand_safe=excluded.step1_grounded_brand_safe, home_route=excluded.home_route, distinctiveness=excluded.distinctiveness, register=excluded.register, realism_level=excluded.realism_level, render_stack=excluded.render_stack, grade=excluded.grade, motion_feel=excluded.motion_feel, ip_flags=excluded.ip_flags, gate_con